        -:   83:/// Submits a completion token or function object for execution.
        -:   84:/**
        -:   85: * This function submits an object for execution using the specified executor.
        -:   86: * The function object may be called from the current thread prior to returning
        -:   87: * from <tt>dispatch()</tt>. Otherwise, it is queued for execution.
        -:   88: *
        -:   89: * @param ex The target executor.
        -:   90: *
        -:   91: * @param token The @ref completion_token that will be used to produce a
        -:   92: * completion handler. The function signature of the completion handler must be:
        -:   93: * @code void handler(); @endcode
        -:   94: *
        -:   95: * @returns This function returns <tt>async_initiate<NullaryToken,
        -:   96: * void()>(Init{ex}, token)</tt>, where @c Init is a function object type
        -:   97: * defined as:
        -:   98: *
        -:   99: * @code class Init
        -:  100: * {
        -:  101: * public:
        -:  102: *   using executor_type = Executor;
        -:  103: *   explicit Init(const Executor& ex) : ex_(ex) {}
        -:  104: *   executor_type get_executor() const noexcept { return ex_; }
        -:  105: *   template <typename CompletionHandler>
        -:  106: *     void operator()(CompletionHandler&& completion_handler) const;
        -:  107: * private:
        -:  108: *   Executor ex_; // exposition only
        -:  109: * }; @endcode
        -:  110: *
        -:  111: * The function call operator of @c Init:
        -:  112: *
        -:  113: * @li Obtains the handler's associated executor object @c ex1 of type @c Ex1 by
        -:  114: * performing @code auto ex1 = get_associated_executor(handler, ex); @endcode
        -:  115: *
        -:  116: * @li Obtains the handler's associated allocator object @c alloc by performing
        -:  117: * @code auto alloc = get_associated_allocator(handler); @endcode
        -:  118: *
        -:  119: * @li If <tt>execution::is_executor<Ex1>::value</tt> is true, constructs a
        -:  120: * function object @c f with a member @c executor_ that is initialised with
        -:  121: * <tt>prefer(ex1, execution::outstanding_work.tracked)</tt>, a member @c
        -:  122: * handler_ that is a decay-copy of @c completion_handler, and a function call
        -:  123: * operator that performs:
        -:  124: * @code auto a = get_associated_allocator(handler_);
        -:  125: * prefer(executor_, execution::allocator(a)).execute(std::move(handler_));
        -:  126: * @endcode
        -:  127: *
        -:  128: * @li If <tt>execution::is_executor<Ex1>::value</tt> is false, constructs a
        -:  129: * function object @c f with a member @c work_ that is initialised with
        -:  130: * <tt>make_work_guard(ex1)</tt>, a member @c handler_ that is a decay-copy of
        -:  131: * @c completion_handler, and a function call operator that performs:
        -:  132: * @code auto a = get_associated_allocator(handler_);
        -:  133: * work_.get_executor().dispatch(std::move(handler_), a);
        -:  134: * work_.reset(); @endcode
        -:  135: *
        -:  136: * @li If <tt>execution::is_executor<Ex>::value</tt> is true, performs
        -:  137: * @code prefer(ex, execution::allocator(alloc)).execute(std::move(f)); @endcode
        -:  138: *
        -:  139: * @li If <tt>execution::is_executor<Ex>::value</tt> is false, performs
        -:  140: * @code ex.dispatch(std::move(f), alloc); @endcode
        -:  141: *
        -:  142: * @par Completion Signature
        -:  143: * @code void() @endcode
        -:  144: */
